> |---|---|---|---|
> | 1 | §4.3, "Limits of the statement", "Range and sample size" | The figure $2.9\cdot10^{26}$ given for (b) is the sample size of the computation referee's variant of (b), with cover radius $\varepsilon/24$ and factor $72$. The version of (b) stated here, with radius $\varepsilon/32$ and factor $32$, needs about $4.4\cdot10^{26}$ by the same cover formula | Fixed: both figures are given, each with its version and source. Re-evaluated at finalization with the cover formula of `../checks/verify-RT-tube-computation/v_sample_size.py`: $4.43\cdot10^{26}$ against $2.92\cdot10^{26}$ at $L=2$, and $7.4\cdot10^{55}$ against $1.6\cdot10^{55}$ at $L=3$ |
